 but  i really felt like my experience this  time around mirrored that of lena's  experience trying to fit herself back  into this family trying to become master  i really felt like it was it was a  discovery and every single day i was  learning things from brent i was  learning things from sadie and kennedy  it was learning things from my old  script and the notes that i had made  when i was 10 um but i i really felt  like confident in the fact that i could  do it i could  step back into her shoes and like  recreate this character but i think  there was also a conscious effort to try  and not try and mimic exactly what i did  in the first movie find her again find  who she is and then bring something new  to it and i think we did that  really well william i know that there  was some talk about  not bringing um isabelle back to play  esther  and you fought for her can you talk a  little bit about  what the reasoning  behind  not bringing her back would have been  and just like i personally can't see  anybody playing esther  and  it seems ridiculous but you know no i  hear you and  i think at first just because so much  time had gone by i had no idea if she  ever you know if she would have been  like you're crazy i'm not going to  pretend to be a kid in the movie you  know she may have said that if i would  have asked her directly she actually  approached me sort of  and and then she was like so passionate  about the fact that this is my character  i just want you to know and if there's  any way we can make it work i want to  keep telling her story  and i was like wow that's that's the  biggest  hurdle is her like genuinely wanting to  do it  and um  so for me then it was it was just like  that's because that's the hardest part  like it's lightning in a bottle to find  a kid like she was in  2008  um  that could do that that could play that  kind of character  and then it's such a specific character  she's so iconic that it was very  difficult for me to imagine anybody else  and certainly  hindsight impossible in any way to  imagine anybody else because we were  able to do it and then once we get into  doing it  you know there were so many small  nuances  and aspects of the character that she  could do that it would have it you know  it just  i agree with you you know it just would  never have been the same thing and um  you know which is what's cool about  doing it once  means that if we ever wanted to do it  again we can do it again you know it's  like it's she'll never grow out of the  character  um it's really but about you know her  like if she wants to do it right but um  and then and then getting it getting it  approved or whatever it took us about  you know on and off  like nearly a year  of of tests and  and  a lot of conversations and a lot of  spitballing and brainstorming and um  and then ultimately you know  the final test we did where she actually  came in and dressed up like esther for  the first time in a decade i guess  um  and it was kind of a nutty little shoot  that  you know it it did its job you know it  allowed us to kind of tell the story  with her as a character again and it was  and that was it then we were off to the  races and making the movie together  which was i actually like dm'd  brent when he got signed on to be the  director and i went to his boy premiere  party because i was like  i have to stand in front of him so he  sees that it's not that crazy of an idea  that i could come back because  you know obviously you grow up but my my  i always joke like i grew into my face  like my face was always a little bit  bigger than the rest of my body i was  like i still have the same face  and it didn't i mean it seemed natural  that  you would if you're playing  if you're an adult you know if you're  playing  you know  you know i was talking to the director  of photography and he made a good point  and i don't know that we ever even  talked about this but he said  he's like in this movie  she looks probably more like she should  have looked in the first movie like  because this is really who she is you  know she's this petite ultra petite  um youthful looking adult  and um  so  yeah it's pretty crazy and uh isabel you  were an associate producer on this film  um  did that come with any kind of  um extra  like what did that entail for you i  think it was more so just being  creatively involved in more aspects of  bringing her back and i think  you know we just brett and i just had  way more of a collaborative i would say  conversations about things to bring from  the last movie into this one  whether that was like articles of  clothing or  even things that we wanted to do with  the doubles with kennedy and sadie you  know it was more like i got to be  creatively involved in not just you know  the creation of this character but like  how do we  how do we create something new and fresh  together and you know it  i i've never played that role before  being an associate producer it was  definitely like learning every single  day but i i just felt like i was  involved in the movie from the very  beginning in the sense that  i had talked to david leslie johnson our  executive producer before the movie even  kind of got put together and it was a  conversation of whether or not i could  come back and play esther how i could  creatively be involved as a consultant  things like that so i think in any way i  would have probably been been involved  in some capacity but to be able to  reprise this role as well as be involved  in some of the you know creative choices  and be able to collaborate with brent  and with alex and  david and everyone really it was just  such a cool experience to have and for  this movie too i mean this was the first  film that i did when i was a kid so to  come back  to this like family it was really  special and i'll tell you  for me um  in that respect  once we started really working together  and then there were questions in the  script that i was